== Optional ==
Easier to read
-> Avoid NullPointerException

Optional.of(o) -> object (don't catch NullPointerException)
Optional.ofNullable(o) -> object or Optional.empty
Optional.orElse(o) -> object or else another object
Optional.isPresent(action) -> if isn't null, do the action

It's created to use as a type of return, but isn't recommended as a parameter or an attribute